---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
const updated = 'July 2026';
---
<Base title="Terms of Use" description="Terms of use for Tomatick and tomatick.us: what the app does, how you may use it, and the limits that apply." path="/terms/">
  <div class="container-page py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="doc">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>The software</h2>
      <p>
        Tomatick is free, open-source software released under the
        <a href="https://github.com/MichalAFerber/tomatick/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MIT License</a>.
        Your use, copying, modification and distribution of the software are governed by that license,
        which also states that the software is provided <strong>“as is”, without warranty of any kind</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        tomatick.us provides information and downloads for the Tomatick app. We aim to keep it accurate and
        available but make no guarantees of uptime, fitness for a particular purpose, or freedom from errors.
        Download links point to release artifacts hosted on GitHub.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Don't use the site to distribute malware or misrepresent the project.</li>
        <li>Don't attempt to disrupt or gain unauthorized access to the site or its infrastructure.</li>
        <li>The Tomatick and TechGuyWithABeard names and logos remain the property of their owner; the MIT license covers the code, not the brand marks.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, the authors and copyright holders are not liable for any
        claim, damages, or other liability arising from the software or the use of this website.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated from time to time; the “last updated” date above reflects the latest revision.
        Questions? See the <a href={SITE.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
